{"id": "EUVD-2026-86945", "enisaUuid": "32436288-fb71-3f9f-8d57-9f0bada1c3cd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: propagate DACL parsing errors\n\nparse_dacl() silently accepts truncated ACEs and allocation failures,\nallowing set_info_sec() to continue with an incomplete ACL conversion.\n\nReturn parsing and allocation errors to parse_sec_desc() so malformed\nsecurity descriptors are rejected before inode attributes or ACL xattrs\nare updated.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:36:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/99ae165acf633b13df34105815110fec332a2cdc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/461f10a5297e85b7c1cd21838922f2e57b934d2d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/37952f03d5171eb3a33b2abc2cf6e456d69ff4a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a04dac1f2cffe9533f4260f0659297d805e69194", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c61dc7b1b4a3234b4aa3965502908a292238805c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98114", "GHSA-fpg3-37rc-jhfw"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01fca541-c380-30e1-973b-cbaeced6e666", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "29d41506-d9fd-3a2f-9b43-7d6ed802031c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <c61dc7b1b4a3234b4aa3965502908a292238805c"}, {"id": "666345c7-46ff-3b84-a168-18c6b38af970", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <37952f03d5171eb3a33b2abc2cf6e456d69ff4a1"}, {"id": "75c1706d-fe7b-3ce0-bc63-5ddaaf2bd333", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "81e1a85a-d8e1-32dd-a0a0-78174bcca760", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <461f10a5297e85b7